; The C stubs are split across platform #if arms (see
; lib/olly_common/max_rss_stubs.c), where a bad edit can detach an arm and
; leave the wrong platform's code compiled in. That fails at runtime rather
; than at build time, and the only diagnostic is an unused-function warning
; for the code that got orphaned — so promote that class to an error.
;
; Dev profile only: opam builds with --profile release, and a released
; package should not break on whatever warning a future compiler invents.

(env
 (dev
  (c_flags
   (:standard
    -Wall
    -Werror=unused-function
    -Werror=implicit-function-declaration))))
